/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  unsteady06_reactor_fill_and_react -- a reactor with a LEVEL fills from a
  heel while it reacts (C205, slice 2: dynamicCSTR with `volumeMode variable`).

  The constant-volume dynamicCSTR cannot start empty: its volume is a number
  you type and F_out = F_in.  Here the liquid inventory is the state, the
  volume is derived from it on the case's package and the level is that
  volume over a declared vertical cylinder (D = 0.5 m, H = 1.0 m):

      dn_i/dt = ndot_in,i - F_out x_i + sum_r nu_i r_r V
      V = sum n_i MW_i / rho(T, P, x)         h = V / (pi D^2 / 4)

  The outflow is DECLARED: `mode flow`, F_out = 0, so the vessel only fills.
  Feed: pure isobutanol, F = 1.0e-3 kmol/s, k = 4.0e-4 1/s (constant: Ea = 0),
  starting from a 0.02 m heel.  An isomerisation changes no moles, and a
  first-order law makes the extent rate k n_A independent of the volume, so
  the mole numbers have an EXACT closed form while the volume keeps growing:

      n_A(t) = F/k + (n_A0 - F/k) exp(-k t)
      n_B(t) = n_A0 + n_B0 + F t - n_A(t)
      M(t)   = M0 + MW F t        (both isomers have the same MW)
      V(t)   = M(t) / rho         h(t) = V(t) / area
      c_A    = n_A / V

  check_dynamic_cstr_level recomputes these from the declared numbers and
  holds the run to them (the density is the run's own column: it moves a
  little with T, because the isomerisation is mildly exothermic).

  ENERGY.  Both species carry a formation datum, so the vessel takes the
  CANONICAL route (announced at start-up): it stores H on the elements datum,
  the heat of reaction is a consequence of it, the outlet term cancels, and
  the ledger CLAIMS mass and energy and closes.  Compare ctrl22, the same
  reactor with a level loop and a temperature loop together.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        dynamicCSTR;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( product );

        operation
        {
            volumeMode  variable;

            geometry
            {
                shape       verticalCylinder;
                diameter    0.5 m;              // area 0.19635 m2
                height      1.0 m;              // the overflow level
            }

            outflow
            {
                mode        flow;
                F           0.0 kmol/s;         // nothing leaves: the vessel FILLS
            }
        }

        reaction    isobutanol_to_2butanol;
    }
);
